<main class="pi-content">

    <section class="pi-hero fade-up fade-up-1">
        <p class="pi-eyebrow">Open Parachute, PBC &middot; 2026</p>
        <h1>Own your compute.<br>Own your AI.<br><em>Own your data.</em></h1>
        <p class="pi-lede">Parachute is self-hosted personal-AI infrastructure &mdash; opinionated, modular, and yours.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-section fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p class="pi-label">The problem</p>
        <h2 class="pi-headline">AI is getting personal.<br>The infrastructure isn't.</h2>
        <div class="pi-body">
            <p>The AI you use is becoming the most intimate software in your life. It sees your work, your voice notes, your half-formed thinking. The places that data lives are someone else's database, on someone else's terms, with someone else's incentives.</p>
            <p>Every model vendor is racing to add memory, agents, and integrations &mdash; on their server, in their format, locked to their product. The pattern is familiar, and the destination is the same: <strong>your context becomes their moat</strong>.</p>
            <p>The alternative isn't no-AI. It's AI that runs against infrastructure you own.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-section fade-up fade-up-3">
        <p class="pi-label">The Parachute approach</p>
        <h2 class="pi-headline">Modular.<br>Self-hosted.<br>Opinionated by default.</h2>
        <div class="pi-body">
            <ol class="pi-num-list">
                <li>
                    <span class="pi-num">1</span>
                    <div class="pi-num-body">
                        <strong>Small modules over one big platform</strong>
                        <span>A vault, a transcriber, a notes app, a hub. Each is independently useful, written to a shared module protocol. You can run one, all, or swap any of them out.</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="pi-num">2</span>
                    <div class="pi-num-body">
                        <strong>Self-hosted by default, cloud as a convenience</strong>
                        <span>The whole stack runs on your laptop or your server. We also offer a managed cloud for the same code &mdash; not because you have to, because we want to.</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="pi-num">3</span>
                    <div class="pi-num-body">
                        <strong>Open standards, not lock-in</strong>
                        <span>Built on MCP for AI access, OAuth for delegation, JSON Schema for module config. Any AI client, any agent, any UI you want to build on top.</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="pi-num">4</span>
                    <div class="pi-num-body">
                        <strong>One sign-in, narrowed by scope</strong>
                        <span>The hub is the front door. It issues scope-narrowed JWTs to clients and agents, so each one gets exactly the access it needs &mdash; nothing more.</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-section fade-up fade-up-4">
        <p class="pi-label">What ships today</p>
        <h2 class="pi-headline">Five modules, all installable<br>with one command.</h2>
        <div class="pi-body">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.75rem;"><code>parachute install &lt;module&gt;</code> &mdash; the hub coordinates lifecycle, OAuth, and the service catalog across the rest.</p>
            <div class="pi-modules">
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                    <h3>Vault</h3>
                    <p>The knowledge graph. SQLite-backed, REST + MCP, wikilinks, full-text and semantic search, Obsidian import/export.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                    <h3>Scribe</h3>
                    <p>Whisper-compatible transcription API. Runs locally by default; bring your own cloud provider if you want one.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                    <h3>Notes</h3>
                    <p>Browser-based companion for the Vault. Installable PWA, works offline, voice capture with auto-transcription.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                    <h3>Hub</h3>
                    <p>The coordinator. Install, start, stop, expose; OAuth issuer with scope-narrowed JWTs and a per-module admin UI.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag exploration">Exploration</span>
                    <h3>Paraclaw</h3>
                    <p>A Parachute distribution &mdash; a fork of NanoClaw with vault integration, exploring an opinionated all-in-one experience.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-mod">
                    <span class="pi-mod-tag">Patterns</span>
                    <h3>Module protocol</h3>
                    <p>Cross-cutting conventions: <code>info</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>services.json</code>, <code>well-known</code>. The contract third-party modules will plug into.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-section fade-up fade-up-5">
        <p class="pi-label">Parachute Cloud</p>
        <h2 class="pi-headline">The done-for-you path.<br>Same code, same exits.</h2>
        <div class="pi-body">
            <p>Most people don't want to run a server. Parachute Cloud is the hosted version of the same modules &mdash; managed vault, multi-device sync, cloud transcription, no setup. You bring your AI client; we run the infrastructure.</p>
            <div class="pi-tiers">
                <div class="pi-tier">
                    <div class="pi-tier-price">Free<span>&nbsp;</span></div>
                    <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Self-host</strong> &mdash; all modules, AGPL, run anywhere</div>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-tier featured">
                    <div class="pi-tier-price">~$5<span>/mo</span></div>
                    <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Cloud</strong> &mdash; managed vault + transcription, multi-device sync, OAuth-gated public exposure</div>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-tier">
                    <div class="pi-tier-price">Custom<span>&nbsp;</span></div>
                    <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Org / pro</strong> &mdash; team vaults, private deployments, extended modules</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Same shape as self-hosted. Export everything, leave at any time. The cloud is a convenience, not a lock-in.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-section fade-up fade-up-6">
        <p class="pi-label">Why now</p>
        <h2 class="pi-headline">The infrastructure layer is suddenly tractable.</h2>
        <div class="pi-body">
            <div class="pi-why">
                <div class="pi-why-card">
                    <strong>MCP is real.</strong>
                    <span>An open protocol for AI to talk to tools, supported by every major lab. The integration layer is no longer proprietary.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-why-card">
                    <strong>Local models work.</strong>
                    <span>Transcription, embeddings, and small LLMs run on a laptop today. Self-hosting isn't a sacrifice anymore.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-why-card">
                    <strong>People feel the lock-in.</strong>
                    <span>The cost of pouring your context into a closed product is becoming legible. Trust is the differentiator.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-why-card">
                    <strong>The ecosystem is small.</strong>
                    <span>Self-hostable, AI-native infrastructure is a clear shape that almost no one is building. The window to define it is open.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">We're a Colorado Public Benefit Corporation. Open source isn't a distribution strategy &mdash; it's the only honest answer to "why should I trust you with this?"</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pi-close fade-up fade-up-6">
        <p class="pi-close-quote">Personal-AI infrastructure, owned by the person.</p>
